## Language tokenization

VitePress uses `Intl.Segmenter` to segment Chinese and Japanese characters in supported environments.

When unavailable, the fallback uses ordinary splitting and may provide reduced matching accuracy.

Custom tokenization can override this behavior.

Preserve native language handling unless an explicit supported override is requested.

## Search document IDs

Search document IDs use site-relative paths such as:

`/guide/page.html#section`

They do not include the configured site `base`.

VitePress resolves the `base` when rendering search results.

Make sure customizations do not accidentally duplicate or omit the base path.

